#
# Counter-example for the math:PersistenceMorphism frame (issue #1527): a
# math:PersistenceMorphism naming its math:morphismSource but omitting its
# math:morphismTarget — a map of persistence modules that names only one endpoint. The
# min-1 qualified restriction on math:morphismTarget derives a sh:qualifiedMinCount
# property shape, so validation MUST emit shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent and
# NO other finding (math:IncompletePersistenceMorphism).
# ISOLATION: the math:morphismSource arm is satisfied by a well-formed math:PersistenceModule
# (naming its math:moduleIndex and math:structureMap so math:IncompletePersistenceModule stays
# silent), so only the math:morphismTarget arm fires.
# Back-reference: math:IncompletePersistenceMorphism (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecPersistenceMorphismNoTarget).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:morphism a math:PersistenceMorphism ;
    math:morphismSource ex:sourceModule .        # names the source but NO math:morphismTarget

ex:sourceModule a math:PersistenceModule ;
    math:moduleIndex ex:indexPoset ;
    math:structureMap ex:transition .
ex:indexPoset a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:transition a math:MathematicalObject .
